Fig. 1.   Chemical structures and biosynthesis of PUFAs. (A) Structures of 
docosahexaenoic acid (DHA; C22:6 ω3), docosapentaenoic acid (DPA; C22:5 ω6), 
eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA; C20:5 ω3), and arachidonic acid (ARA; C20:4 ω6). 
(B) Domain organizations of eukaryotic (Schizochytrium sp.) and prokaryotic (M. 
marina, P. profundum, and A. marina) PUFA synthases. KS, β-­ketoacyl synthase; 
MAT, malonyl CoA transacylase; ACP, acyl carrier protein; KR, β-­ketoacyl reductase; 
DHPKS, polyketide synthase-­type dehydratase; AT, acyltransferase (thioesterase); 
CLF, chain length factor; DHFabA, FabA-­type dehydratase; ER, and enoyl reductase. 
(C) Reactions in a single-­chain elongation cycle of PUFA synthases.
